.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-s3-object-retention-set - Lock an object version


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro s3 object retention set   [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Lock an object version

.PP
Sets or extends the retention of one version (\fBversion_id\fR empty = current) for \fBdays\fR 1-3650 from now. Retention can only be extended; COMPLIANCE cannot be switched to GOVERNANCE. COMPLIANCE cannot be shortened, switched to GOVERNANCE or removed by anyone (Gyro included) until it expires; the data is kept and the service keeps being billed until then, even after cancellation. Send \fB"confirm": true\fR and \fB"acknowledge": "COMPLIANCE"\fR\&.

.PP
API: PUT /cloud/storage/{id}/buckets/{bucket}/objects/retention (operationId setStorageObjectRetention, scope services_write)


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--acknowledge\fP=""
	COMPLIANCE only: type COMPLIANCE

.PP
\fB--data\fP=""
	request body as JSON, @file or @- (stdin)

.PP
\fB--days\fP=0
	days

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	show the price quote / request without changing anything

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for set

.PP
\fB--idempotency-key\fP=""
	idempotency key (automatic for money operations)

.PP
\fB--key\fP=""
	key

.PP
\fB--mode\fP=""
	mode (GOVERNANCE|COMPLIANCE)

.PP
\fB--set\fP=[]
	extra body field key=value (repeatable)

.PP
\fB--version-id\fP=""
	Empty = current version


